[#:seon.task{:name "a-changed-check-builds-a-world-per-request"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A my.test/check of a changed program pays about 1 s in clean-request-handle per request: an overlay write of 480-620 ms and a fresh SCI acquisition of 414-450 ms. A changed one-test check measures 1,485-1,584 ms, a newcomer's one-assertion run 3,456 ms (clean-request-handle 2,527 ms), and prepare-merge! of a one-test delta 4.06 s. Recommended: fold the overlay into the checkpoint keyed by [base cluster effective process overlay-digest], so a request is a branch! plus a base-context hit."
             :must-read #{seon.test/clean-request-handle seon.test/prepare-checkpoint! seon.test/run}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-dogfood-newcomer-astra-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-test-request-cost-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-test-selection-cost-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/test-world-preparation-spends-seconds-in-config-apply-and-unmemoized-reads.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "check-fails-on-agent-registered-schemas"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Once any contract on a branch names a schema the agent registered, my.test/check fails every test on the branch with :malli.core/invalid-schema {:schema :notes-index/note}: the check world's fork (fork-cluster-ctx via clean-request-handle -> install-function-contract!) builds contracts against a projection without the branch's schemas, while the install gate uses the right one. 1.6-3.2 s, once 17.3 s."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/install-function-contract! seon.test/clean-request-handle}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-author-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/my-test-check-fails-every-test-once-a-branch-contract-names-an-agent-schema.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-check-with-nothing-to-run-answers-green"
             :kind :function
             :intent "my.test/check answers green when the changed symbol has no executable reaching test, e.g. a caller dropped at acquisition (dogfood #20): the change goes untested and the answer says pass. Missing coverage must refuse by name."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run seon.test/select}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-report-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-agent-run-stability-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-world-has-no-agent"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A REPL deftest's member world contains no agent entity and no :seon.agent/id, so an agent-scoped call such as (my.task/steps {}) is untestable (only refusal paths are). Seeding the agent costs 88 ms (creation-tx); acquiring with an agent id 626 ms against 31 ms. Owner ruling: seed the executing agent, or branch the world from the agent's own commit (which deletes the checkpoint and overlay machinery, about 200 lines)."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.agent/creation-tx seon.test/clean-request-handle}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-report-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/agent-test-worlds-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/an-agents-test-world-has-no-agent-so-my-functions-cannot-be-tested-as-documented.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "property-members-pay-a-commit-per-step"
             :kind :function
             :intent "turn-test's recovery, transitions and virtual members take 17-18 s each against the 5 s bound, because each step is a file-store commit (48-96 ms; an in-memory commit is 5 ms). Recommended: member worlds as in-memory branches of one prepared commit (the fast-harness slice)."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-turn-test-reds-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/turn-test-property-members-pay-a-file-store-commit-per-step.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "tests-redefine-default-vars"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "About 300 with-redefs / alter-var-root sites in test/ redefine default's Vars JVM-wide; e.g. fn_test.clj:1067's with-redefs of analyzer/analyze made a concurrent read-only analyze-entities throw 'analysis must not run', and a concurrent publication or write-back fails the same way. Substitute effects as explicit values in injected worlds. Census by clj-kondo analysis (2026-09-27): 303 call sites (with-redefs 208, with-redefs-fn 47, intern 23, alter-var-root 17, load-file 8) binding 404 Var replacements across 96 files; top targets seon.ai/complete 56, seon.db/transact! 14, seon.sci.kernel/invoke 10, seon.sci.eval/evaluate 10, seon.db/q 10. The seam per target and the tests each converts are in the evidence note's seam census."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/merge-ns-rows-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/test-agents-concurrency-2026-09-27.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/eval-test-with-redefs-of-packaged-forms-breaks-concurrent-publication.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "checks-write-into-live-custody"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The auto-check and gate bodies write into the agent's live branch; functions keep their creation context's connection, so forking alone cannot move their calls (Astra M2; owner decision on gate world pending)."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/agent-path-2-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "reuse-only-selection-costs-a-second"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A named request whose members are all reusable greens still pays about 1.2 s before answering: seon.fault-test on default, 8 members, 0 executed, 1,223 ms wall; profiled, selection-admission 1,178 ms of which selection-facts 1,015 ms (4 calls), with-declarations x1,363. At six concurrent requests selection averaged 2,483 ms. Done when a request answering only recorded greens answers in time proportional to its members (tens of ms), measured by the same probe."
             :must-read #{seon.test/selection-admission seon.test/selection-facts}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/test-agents-concurrency-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "one-test-run-costs-seconds-around-a-147-ms-body"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.test/run of ONE named test costs 4.7 s cold and 2.2 s warm on default (2026-09-28, pid 77505, seon.sci.eval-test/require-context-entities-carry-namespace-symbols) while its body (seon.test/member-result) takes 147 ms. Profiled cold: seon.test/select 1,274 ms (selection-facts 1,092 ms x4, 239 seon.db/q and 786 with-declarations calls), 8 transactions 1,786 ms (encode-call-output-in 1,220 ms x7), clean-request-handle 1,532 ms (fork-cluster-ctx 553 ms, seed-cluster-facts! 500 ms, config apply-compiled! 409 ms), program-written-since? 1,096 ms. Warm: select 1,336 ms, transactions 524 ms, clean-request-handle 362 ms. The one-path proofs pay this per run (v1-red-delta 13.5 s for three runs). Done when a one-test run under a test agent (S12: the defn's batch schedules it, its settle records the result) answers in well under a second, measured by the same probe."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run seon.test/select seon.test/clean-request-handle seon.test.runner/program-written-since?}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/one-repl-path-spec-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-branch-test-run-cannot-branch-its-fresh-checkpoint"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(my.test/run-owned {:seon.ns/name 'my.e1probe}) from MCP agent e1-probe (hosted on :agent-665a30c12282) refused three times on default fb1437312 (2026-09-28, 2.2-5.1 s, 325k-435k armed calls each): no branch or commit <fresh checkpoint head> to branch from (:seon.cluster.registry/source-absent, request branch :agent-...). The same prepare-checkpoint! -> open-overlay! -> branch! sequence by hand from the default instance's store succeeds in 840 ms. The agent branch's world base is the stale adopted commit 6abadd62 while the cluster records 6abae0f5, so each request prepares a new checkpoint and retires the other checkpoint-default-* ones. Every such run also carried a diagnostic: seon.turn.batch/join-write refused its own output contract (:seon.batch/join). No agent on its own branch can prove a task, so no fault it fixes ever closes. Done when that run answers the test's red result and a regression runs a named test from a hosted agent branch."
             :must-read #{seon.test/clean-request-handle seon.test/prepare-checkpoint! seon.test/run my.test/run-owned}
             :evidence #{"tmp/health-loop-proof/evidence.md"}}

 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-request-refuses-whole-when-one-namespace-has-no-eligible-tests"
             :kind :function
             :intent "bin/test refuses the whole request when one namespace has no eligible tests, and does not name it; repl-parity-test reports \"no eligible tests\" without a reason. Done when the refusal names the namespace and why (no deftest, all excluded, unarmed) and the other namespaces run, and repl-parity-test's cause is stated."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-run-refusal-escapes-as-an-exception"
             :kind :function
             :intent "When a throwaway JVM's test run hit the roster refusal (seon.cluster.store/open-branch!), seon.test/run let it escape as a raw exception, so bin/test-check showed 'PREPL evaluation failed' instead of an error value naming the refusal (lane check-flake, 2026-10-06). CLAUDE.md: the test runner is an entrant boundary; any exception reaching it becomes the one error value, recorded as a fault and delivered as data. Done when an acquisition refusal inside seon.test/run returns its declared error alternative and the check output names it."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "release-and-rethrow-sites-repeat-instead-of-one-with-release"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "RC9 (tmp/root-cause-census/report.md): test.clj repeats a release-and-rethrow shape seven times. Done when one with-release combinator replaces them and the test still releases resources on setup and cleanup failure."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}
             :evidence #{"tmp/root-cause-census/report.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-transitions-test-runs-six-to-seven-seconds-against-a-five-second-bound"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "The transitions test takes 6.4-7.3 s (bound 5 s): per-transaction projection/encode cost. Done when the responsible armed functions are named from a profile and the test fits its bound without raising it."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/compact!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "red-tests-on-head-are-unclassified"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "The errors-s1 lane found reds on HEAD a5a21fd58 without its diff (baseline runs 940885360cdd and 4f4d5824dfe8): seon.cluster.host-test x5 (including a-refused-deletion-is-associated-only-with-the-one-evaluation-proposing-it, 7 assertions), seon.render.entity-pairs-test x2, seon.render.value-test x2 and seon.rereads-test x2. They block naming whole namespaces in bin/lane commit --test, so slices name single tests instead. CLAUDE.md: classify each red from stored runs by the commit that changed its behavior, then delete a test of deleted machinery, update a retired assumption or fix the surviving owner. Done when each red names its classifying commit and is deleted, converted or fixed (or restated as its own task), and the four namespaces run green on HEAD. Proof: the four namespaces' own tests, run by name on HEAD with zero reds (each kept test named by its classification)."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}
             :evidence #{"tmp/errors/s1-s2-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "test-release-closes-branch-connections-out-of-order"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A test world's release does not own its connections exactly once. (1) The full-tier run of 2026-10-06 (bin/test, tmp/orchestrator/full-run-2.txt) ended in seon.cluster.store/release-store! throwing Datahike's 'Cannot delete a database with active connections. Release them first.' with two agent overlay connections ([:datahike/overlay ...] on :agent-fa3beda720e7 and :agent-1e8be0903fd1) still open; the request escaped as 'PREPL evaluation failed' and the run's tally was lost. (2) An error recorded on default (2026-10-07, signature 7147098166ec, operation seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch! reached from seon.test/release-context!): 'Connection has been released.' (a release after the connection was already released). Done when a test request releases each hosted agent's overlay connection before its store, retire-branch! never runs on a released connection, a full-tier run ends with its tally, and a regression releases a world holding agent overlays. Proof: a new seon.test-test/a-world-holding-agent-overlays-releases-cleanly (to be written first) naming this task."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.agent/release-context! seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch! seon.cluster.store/release-store! seon.test/run}
             :evidence #{"tmp/orchestrator/full-run-2.txt"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "reds-on-head-9d6b392b6-in-task-reaching-tests", :kind :namespace, :intent "Booted from HEAD 9d6b392b6 in a throwaway JVM (runs dd2d7c0063ce, e3c499a59e18), these reds exist without lane task-tags' diff: seon.error.attribution-test/a-definitions-failure-in-an-evaluation-is-its-fault-and-task (the error value carries no :seon.error/producer or :seon.instrument/fn, no fault signature), seon.error.attribution-test/a-batch-failure-names-the-definition-visible-when-it-ran (error), seon.render.ns-test/task-and-schema-entities-render-as-graph-nodes (56 of 200 stored intents exceed 400 characters), seon.task-steps-test/steps-persist-across-a-compaction (compact! answers no :seon.agent/id), seon.cluster.host-test/a-proposal-waits-for-its-assigned-tasks-proofs-then-reaches-root (prepare-merge! answers no :seon.test/passed?, proofs or merge). Done when each is classified by the commit that changed its behavior and fixed, converted or deleted, and the five run green on HEAD.", :must-read #{seon.task/steps! my.program/prepare-merge!}, :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/task-tags/task-tags-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "reds-on-head-178aa24e0-in-db-program-schema-tests"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Booted from HEAD 178aa24e0 in a throwaway JVM (run 8c1ff443a361), these are red without lane task-tags' structural-hash diff: seon.db-test/database-operations-preserve-refusals-at-their-declared-boundary, seon.db-test/query-and-pull-append-evidence-only-when-captured (over its 5 s bound), seon.program-test/a-declaration-added-after-the-first-call-is-a-cache-miss and declaring-an-attribute-on-a-program-entity-schema-is-sufficient (an unregistered attribute schema throws), seon.program-test/indexed-and-evaluated-declarations-are-the-same-entities, opening-basis-divergence-is-only-claimed-when-it-is-measurable, runtime-schema-declarations-project-namespaced-properties, typed-cross-namespace-deletion-retracts-function-and-test, seon.schema-test/a-refused-registration-is-an-error-value-never-a-throw, an-incremental-projection-equals-its-full-build (over its bound), canonical-reference-values-use-the-pull-collection-grammar and every-predicate-schema-declares-what-it-accepts. Done when each is classified by the commit that changed its behavior and fixed, converted or deleted, and they run green on HEAD."
             :must-read #{seon.program/shapes-in seon.schema/register!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/task-tags/task-tags-notes.md"}}]
